group by clause is use to group the records.

syntax: select group by EXPRESSION/Group Function from table [where filter] group by col_name/EXPRESSION;

order of execution:
                        1. From 
                        2. where [if it is present]
                        3. group by (executes row-by-row)
                        4. select (executes group-by-group)

Note: 1. Group by clause is use to group the records.
      2. Group by clause executes row-by-row.
      3. After the execution of group by clause we get the groups.
      4. Therefore any clause that executes after group by clause must executes group-by-group.
      5. The column_name or exression used for grouping can be use for select clause.
      6. Group by clause can be use without using where clause. 
